WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:05.400
Star Wars: The Last Jedi may be a certified
box office hit in the United States, but it

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.090
doesn't hold such a strong distinction overseas.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:12.400
Although the film has held solidly in European
markets, it failed to take hold in the key

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:18.500
blockbuster market of China, pulling in only
$28.7 million over its second place opening

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.500
weekend.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.739
Here's why The Last Jedi struggled in China.

00:00:22.739 --> 00:00:24.089
It's just not as popular

00:00:24.089 --> 00:00:29.859
A large portion of the United States' adult
population in 2017 grew up with the Star Wars

00:00:29.859 --> 00:00:32.189
franchise as a childhood touchstone.

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:37.469
However, in China, the original Star Wars
movies never received a wide theatrical release.

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:41.730
The country's first major introduction to
the franchise came courtesy of the prequel

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:42.730
trilogy.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:46.920
The new trilogy, however, builds heavily on
the mythology and characters introduced in

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.930
the original films, not the prequels.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:53.510
The chance to finally see Luke Skywalker speak
again was enough to draw millions of fans

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:58.890
across the rest of the world, but those moments
didn't hold the same allure for Chinese audiences.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:01.149
The marketing fell short

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:05.300
Disney is well aware that Star Wars doesn't
the same box office traction in China, so

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.390
they've put in a lot of effort over the years
trying to ramp up recognition.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:13.820
This kicked off in the months leading up to
the release of 2015's The Force Awakens, when

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:19.181
the company placed 500 stormtroopers on the
Great Wall and hired pop star Lu Han to be

00:01:19.181 --> 00:01:21.360
an "official ambassador" for the movie.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.490
For The Last Jedi, Disney tried once again
to drum up the buzz they got for The Force

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:26.520
Awakens.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.880
This included a significant number of billboards
and mobile ads, as well as a premiere at the

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:34.369
Shanghai Disney Resort featuring the film's
biggest stars.

00:01:34.369 --> 00:01:39.390
However, ComScore senior media analyst Paul
Dergarabedian believes that it may have been

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:40.909
too little, too late.

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:45.930
"To elevate the brand in China it may be a
matter of consistency more than anything else."

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:50.789
It's worth noting that the standalone Rogue
One: A Star Wars Story also earned a release

00:01:50.789 --> 00:01:56.770
in China, bringing in $32.4 million in its
opening weekend—more than The Last Jedi.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:01.290
That film, however, had the benefit of two
local stars, Donnie Yen and Jiang Wen, who

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:03.890
lured audiences in.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.359
Piracy problems

00:02:05.359 --> 00:02:09.760
The Last Jedi hit theaters on December 14
in the United States, but it wasn't released

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.900
in China until January 5.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:16.650
With a film this highly anticipated, piracy
was obviously a concern, and the fact that

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:20.850
the release date was so much later in China
may have encouraged some fans to catch the

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:24.390
film illegally online instead of paying to
see it in theaters.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:28.660
Although the later release date may have hurt
the film, it was something Disney pushed for.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:32.890
The company was said to have initially been
offered a release date closer to the U.S.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:37.380
debut, but they chose to avoid the crowded
early December box office, which left early

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.180
January as the best option.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:44.020
Strong local competition
Although Disney pushed the release date to

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:48.600
try to avoid competition, they still managed
to throw The Last Jedi up against one of China's

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.400
strongest franchises: The Ex-Files.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:56.340
The third film in the romantic comedy series,
The Ex-Files 3: Return of the Exes, was able

00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:02.370
to beat out The Last Jedi during its second
week in theaters, pulling in $86.7 million

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:05.360
to The Last Jedi's $28.7 million.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.650
Regardless of why The Last Jedi flopped in
China, there's no need to be concerned about

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:11.760
the film's ultimate box office fate.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:16.210
It earned the second-highest opening of all
time in North America, behind only The Force

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:20.760
Awakens, and managed to beat out Disney's
wildly popular Beauty and the Beast to become

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:25.370
the highest-grossing film of 2017, despite
only being in theaters for two weeks before

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:26.370
the end of the year.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:32.960
It also managed to cross $1 billion worldwide,
sitting it at just over $1.2 billion as of

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:38.120
the making of this video—good for the all-time
13th highest-grossing film worldwide.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:42.420
The Last Jedi may not be doing well in China,
but Disney has nothing to worry about when

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:44.960
it comes to the film's overall performance.

